From: WinBoat
Subject: [PATCH] d3d10umd, d3d9umd, nine, virgl: feature level 11_1, complete Direct3D 9 driver, DXVA2 video processing

Part 1: Direct3D 11 optional features (stage A of docs/gpu-roadmap-todo.md)
- Doubles: the DXBC double instructions (dadd, dmul, dmin, dmax, comparisons, dmov/dmovc, dtof/ftod, and 11.1's
  ddiv, dfma, drcp, dtoi/dtou/itod/utod) and 64-bit immediates, reported when the host's GL has
  ARB_gpu_shader_fp64. virglrenderer translates one double per instruction and negates their 32-bit halves, so
  each double goes through a temporary (DNEG/DABS for modifiers, immediates moved first: it applies an immediate's
  swizzle twice), and every double is computed before the destination is written (in-place ftod).
  32-bit results go to the enabled components in order.
- Logic operations in the output merger (11.1 blend states).
- Feature level 11_1 when the host can: target-independent rasterization and UAV-only rendering with a forced
  sample count (gallium's new pipe_rasterizer_state::forced_sample_count; virgl sends it with
  VIRGL_CCMD_SET_RASTER_SAMPLES when the host announces VIRGL_CAP_V2_RASTER_SAMPLES: WinBoat's virglrenderer
  patch 0004), the output merger's UAVs in every graphics stage, ClearView on typed UAVs. A framebuffer without
  views (UAV-only rendering) gets D3D's largest size (GL calls it incomplete otherwise).
  WINBOAT_D3D_FL11_1=0 leaves 11_1 out. Direct2D uses it: geometry is rendered with 16 forced samples into an
  R16_UINT target with logic op XOR, then composited.

Fixes found on the way:
- SV_ClipDistance was never applied: clip_plane_enable stayed 0, and one declaration (o1.xyzw) counted as one
  distance. The properties count components now, and every draw binds a rasterizer variant enabling the last
  vertex stage's clip distances (GL must not enable unwritten ones). Direct2D clips each geometry of a batch to
  its rectangle that way.
- GDI drawing through IDXGISurface1::GetDC was lost when the app's drawing on the surface wasn't submitted yet:
  the runtime calls DXGI's ResolveSharedResource (a stub) instead of flushing. It flushes now.
- The parser accepts 4-component 64-bit immediates.
- DXGI_FORMAT_B4G4R4A4_UNORM (11.1), the host has it.

Part 2: Direct3D 9 and 10 as complete drivers (stage A2)
- Flip model presents (D3DSWAPEFFECT_FLIPEX) crashed in the runtime (DdBltLH, NULL kernel handle): without a 16-bit
  display mode format the runtime's DirectX 8 HAL check (GetDX8HALCaps) marks the adapter as having no hardware
  primary and makes no driver surface for the desktop. R5G6B5 is a display mode now (only one 16-bit format may
  be: with X1R5G5B5 too, FetchDirectDrawData refuses the driver).
- Exclusive full screen: SetDisplayMode; flip chains are one resource with a surface per subresource; only the
  first allocation of a CreateResource joins the runtime's resource (a second AllocateCb on it bugchecks 0x113/7).
- Shared surfaces opened by a second D3D9 device read black: nine cleared the opened render target at creation.
- virgl: READ|WRITE maps of staged textures became read-only staging maps and dropped the writes (LockRect on render
  targets, GetDC drawing on D3D9 surfaces, D3D10/11 Map(READ_WRITE) after GPU work).
- DXVA2 video processing (video.cpp): progressive and bob processors, YUY2/UYVY/NV12/RGB input, BT.601/709/240M,
  studio and full range, scaling, background; YUV surfaces are textures holding the bytes as they are (packed
  formats as A8R8G8B8 of half width, NV12 as L8 with the chroma rows below), converted by a shader model 3 pass
  and scaled with StretchRect; StretchRect from YUV surfaces, ColorFill and locks on them.
- DepthFill, ResolveSharedResource, UpdateSubresourceUP, GetInfo and the VCACHE query, counter queries (none),
  the Windows 8.1 interface's entry points; ATOC (alpha to coverage) offered.
- The user-mode DLLs carry the driver package's version (meson option winboat-driver-version): the runtimes
  reported 0.0.0.0 to applications.
